{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>All the souls of his sons and his daughters, thirty-three.</b> Jacob is not counted in the seventy, and the beginning of the count of the seventy is from Reuben; and you will find from Reuben to Dinah, with Dinah included, they are thirty-two, and Scripture says thirty-three — rather, this is Yocheved, who was born at their entry to Egypt." "<b>And behold,</b> seventy souls are counted in this parashah in four parts, corresponding to the four women. And he mentioned the word נפש in each and every part, and afterwards he gathered them all together and mentioned all seventy in the language of נפש, as it says: ״כל הנפש לבית יעקב הבאה מצרימה שבעים״ — all the souls to the house of Jacob who came to Egypt: seventy. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:45.035425906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}